<Project>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>true</ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>
    <RestorePackagesWithLockFile>true</RestorePackagesWithLockFile>
    <AnalysisLevel>latest</AnalysisLevel>
    <AnalysisMode>Recommended</AnalysisMode>
    <EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>true</EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <!--
      MSB3277 is the Autodesk reference-version-conflict warning. Referencing AcMgd,
      AcCoreMgd and AcDbMgd always produces it because AutoCAD's managed assemblies
      carry .NET Framework identities that conflict with the .NET 8 reference pack.
      The conflict is inherent to the product, not actionable, and is excluded by
      name here rather than by lowering the warning level for everything.
    -->
    <WarningsNotAsErrors>$(WarningsNotAsErrors);MSB3277</WarningsNotAsErrors>
    <MSBuildWarningsAsMessages>$(MSBuildWarningsAsMessages);MSB3277</MSBuildWarningsAsMessages>
    <!--
      Security/correctness rules that must never be silently ignored, even if a
      future change lowers TreatWarningsAsErrors. Rule IDs are listed explicitly;
      no wildcard or category-wide selection is used.
    -->
    <WarningsAsErrors>$(WarningsAsErrors);CA2000;CA2211;CA5350;CA5351;CA5394;CA3001;CA3002;CA3003;CA3004;CA3005;CA3006;CA3007;CA3008;CA3009;CA3010;CA3011;CA3012</WarningsAsErrors>
    <!--
      Explicit rule-ID exclusions, by exact ID only (no wildcards, no
      category-wide selection). Each entry states the concrete reason it cannot be
      satisfied without changing runtime behaviour or the public API:

        CA1031 - 65 sites are deliberate best-effort catch-alls whose whole purpose
                 is to keep AutoCAD responsive when a side write fails (audit sink,
                 CDE sidecar, receipt/seal writes, named-pipe accept loop). The
                 failure is still reported through a result code or a finding at
                 each site; narrowing the catch type would change which failures
                 are swallowed. This is tracked debt, not an accepted design.
                 Do NOT add new catch (Exception) sites - narrow the catch to the
                 exact exception set instead.
        CA1822 - the flagged members are public API on public types
                 (SafetyPolicy.Evaluate, PublishReceipt.ComputePreflightHash,
                 ForgeToolRunner.ToolCatalogJson); making them static is a
                 breaking API change.
        CA1716 - the namespace Forge.Shared is the library's public identity;
                 renaming it is a breaking API change.

      These are the only excluded IDs; every other diagnostic is fatal.
    -->
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CA1031;CA1822;CA1716</NoWarn>
    <Version>0.3.0</Version>
    <Authors>765T</Authors>
    <Company>765T</Company>
    <Product>765T-Forge</Product>
    <Description>MCP server and AutoCAD plugin for metro/AEC drawing production workflows (AutoCAD 2017+).</Description>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2026 765T</Copyright>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/meococ/765T-Forge</RepositoryUrl>
    <NeutralLanguage>en</NeutralLanguage>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
